Hresvelgr projectile pool initialization at 081A4DF0

The original-ROM probe at caller 081A4F20 records r0 = 081A4EA1 after
successful initialization. Anim_SetKeyframes leaves that Thumb link
address in r0. The caller checks only whether it is negative, so port
success returns zero. Clang otherwise sees an undefined success result.

During 119 neutral frames after controller frame 36257, the ROM retains
its projectile pool, resolves projectile impacts, and takes 50 player
life at 0815EB12. The untreated wasm replay keeps all 487 life. The
first contact diverges before any new attack input.
The generated port with this guard reproduced all 12 original-ROM RAM
checkpoints between controller frames 36257 and 37047, including the
projectile count, first hit, position, boss reaction and sampled RNG.

--- a/src/bosses/hresvelgr/Hresvelgr_InitializeProjectilePool.c
+++ b/src/bosses/hresvelgr/Hresvelgr_InitializeProjectilePool.c
@@ -57,4 +57,7 @@
     /* Success falls through without a defined C value. The stock Anim_SetKeyframes
      * returns through r0, leaving its positive Thumb return address for the caller
      * that checks only whether initialization returned a negative value. */
+#ifdef UBFIX
+    return 0;
+#endif
 }
